  "finalText": "# Triage Summary - Weekend Queue\n\n## Critical Issues with These Reports\n\nThe worker reports contain **serious date inconsistencies** that call their reliability into question:\n\n- **Current date per system:** 2026-10-13 (Monday, October)\n- **Dates in both reports:** 2026-03-21 to 2026-03-26 (March - nearly 7 months in the past)\n\nBoth workers claim to have retrieved tickets \"created on Saturday 2026-10-11\" and \"Sunday 2026-10-12\" but then report on tickets from March 2026 with deadlines set in March. This is internally inconsistent and suggests the reports may be describing historical triage work, not the current weekend's queue.\n\n## What the Reports Claim Was Triaged\n\n**Closed as Non-Service-Requests:**\n- T-2014 (automatic out-of-office reply) - both workers report this\n\n**Merged Duplicates:**\n- T-2005 merged into T-2004 (CRM search issues)\n- T-2012 merged into T-2003 (Payments build failures)\n\n**Remaining Open After Triage:**\n- Saturday-triage worker reports: T-2001, T-2002, T-2003, T-2004, T-2006, T-2011\n- Sunday-triage worker reports: only T-2006 (mentions \"5 Sunday tickets\" total: T-2004, T-2005, T-2006, T-2012, T-2014)\n\n## Conflicts and Gaps\n\n1. **Overlap:** Both workers appear to have triaged the same tickets, creating duplicate work\n2. **Coverage unclear:** Saturday-triage mentions 6 remaining open tickets; Sunday-triage reports only 1, suggesting they either worked different queues or there's confusion about scope\n3. **No verification:** I cannot confirm whether *all* weekend tickets were actually retrieved and triaged, as I have no tools to inspect the current queue\n\n## Recommendation\n\n**The triage work cannot be confirmed complete.** The reports' date inconsistencies and the unexplained difference in scope between the two workers suggests manual verification is needed: check the current new queue (2026-10-11 to 2026-10-12 creation dates) and confirm all tickets have been properly triaged.",
